Phase 3 Regression Gates
All tests must run against a disposable Testnet environment or controlled Testnet data. Do not use Mainnet writes for test setup.
Mainnet proof issuer
Valid Pi access token + canonical Owner of the exact Mainnet Internal project → proof issued.
Valid Pi token but no Mainnet public.users row → denied.
Pi token UID does not match the canonical Owner record → denied.
Project is Core → denied.
Project is unapproved, suspended, archived, or not Mainnet → denied.
Browser attempts to supply a forged project UUID, owner UUID or project type → ignored / denied.
Proof contains no Mainnet users.id or owner_albukhr_user_id.
Proof expires within 120 seconds and has a distinct audience/purpose.
Mainnet login issuer v4 still works unchanged.
Testnet proof endpoint
No Testnet session / expired / revoked / wrong-network session → denied.
Testnet session Pi UID hash differs from proof hash → denied.
Project code/type/source UUID mismatch → denied.
Missing or stale private mirror provenance → denied.
Proof with wrong issuer/audience/purpose/network → denied.
Expired, malformed or tampered proof → denied.
Replayed proof ID → denied.
Same proof cannot be transferred to another Testnet user or project.
Core project cannot obtain eligibility, proof ticket, or submit an application.
Application and review
Duplicate open application for one project → denied.
Browser-supplied applicant user ID / status / reviewer ID / approval flag → ignored or rejected.
Owner can list only applications belonging to its Testnet user ID.
Resubmission allowed only for own changes_requested application.
Admin without valid super_admin Testnet session → denied.
Admin scoped away from the project → denied.
Admin sees Owner-submitted fields read-only.
Admin cannot supply or replace applicant identity.
Mainnet Owner link changed or project status suspended after submission → approval denied.
Admin approval updates Testnet projects.owner_user_id, creates the compatible profile and appends history atomically.
Conflicting Testnet owner binding or owner profile → approval denied; no overwrite.
Core is rejected again inside SQL even if Edge Function or UI is bypassed.
Application never updates Mainnet.
